+`thirdparty/moge` is imported only by the standalone MoGe-3 depth worker.
+Set `path_depth` to a local MoGe-3 `model.pt` or an HF repository ID
+(default `Ruicheng/moge-3-vitl`). Set `moge_python` to an interpreter with
+MoGe-3's torch, flex_gemm, utils3d_moge, OpenCV, SciPy and huggingface_hub
+dependencies; an empty value uses the pipeline interpreter. The pinned
+MoGe-3 refiner requires a compatible torch/Triton stack: on the Wulai
+machine it works with torch 2.13.0+cu130, not torch 2.7.1/Triton 3.3.1.
+The worker keeps that stack separate from GLUEMAP's torch 2.7.1+cu128.
+
+Star inference crops away canvas padding before MoGe-3 inference, solves
+the depth shift from each star's backbone focal length, and aligns scale
+using the confident half of valid depth pixels. Padding, invalid MoGe
+pixels and images without sufficient alignment support retain backbone
+depth; backbone poses, intrinsics and confidence remain unchanged.
+
+For an isolated overlay on an existing CUDA-capable environment, create a
+`uv venv --system-site-packages --python /path/to/base/python /path/to/venv`
+and install this checkout with `uv pip install --python /path/to/venv/bin/python
+--no-deps --no-build-isolation -e .`. Install build/runtime dependencies in the
+overlay first; `--no-deps` preserves the base environment's PyTorch build.
+In particular, install the declared `kornia==0.8.2` in the overlay if the base
+has 0.8.3: VGGSfM imports `kornia.utils.grid`, which 0.8.3 no longer provides.
+The `thirdparty` package is checkout-local, so another editable GLUEMAP
+installation in the base environment cannot supply this fork's submodules.
